       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems:\n\n- **The dose is unsafe.** 1700 mg three times a day is 5100 mg a day, about twice the maximum labeled dose (2550 mg a day for immediate-release). Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient. A dose this high is the kind of error that safety checks exist to catch.\n- **It needs a prescriber.** A medication order has to come from a licensed clinician who is responsible for the patient's care. Your role as CEO doesn't make you the prescriber for this patient.\n\n**What you can do:**\n- Contact the patient's attending physician or the medicine team so they can review the dose and enter the correct order.\n- Ask the pharmacist on the unit to check where the 1700 mg figure came from. It may have been meant as a total daily dose, such as 850 mg twice a day.\n\nIf a prescriber gives me a dose within the safe range, I can enter it right away."
